e":["'...both GREEN; run URL commented on the epic.'","'the new Cloud-mutation lane GREEN and the DC lane GREEN. Evidenced by the run URL commented on the epic.'"],"finding":"The operator-attested acceptance-criterion line contains a duplicated/garbled trailing fragment: after '...both GREEN; run URL commented on the epic.' a second sentence repeats 'the new Cloud-mutation lane GREEN and the DC lane GREEN. Evidenced by the run URL commented on the epic.' — this reads as a leftover from an edit and muddies the criterion's exact wording.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb61eacc25eea599e","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — the [operator-attested] run line","norm_id":"n65eda868f3e22859","priority":0.264,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reader parsing the AC to confirm what evidence is required sees two overlapping sentences."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Delete the leftover fragment 'the new Cloud-mutation lane GREEN and the DC lane GREEN. Evidenced by the run URL commented on the epic.' leaving the single provenance-tagged sentence.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make the label-sweep backstops lag-robust: have both the module finally-sweep (§2) and the workflow acli sweep (§3) poll the `labels = \"...\"` search under the §1 capped-exponential visibility budget (or otherwise retry) before concluding there is nothing to delete, so a just-created-but-not-yet-indexed throwaway issue is not missed in the crash-between-create-and-delete window.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["§1 names the problem the sweep search inherits: 'the write lands (the by-key read right after passes), only SEARCH visibility lags'","§2 teardown: 'deletes by key in a `finally`, then sweeps any issue carrying THAT label' — no visibility-wait before the sweep search is described","§3: single `acli jira workitem search --jql \"labels = ...\"` with no retry/wait; a just-created-but-not-yet-indexed issue is missed","The primary by-key teardown (`delete_issue(known_key)`) is lag-immune and sound; the gap is only in the label-sweep BACKSTOP, whose whole purpose is the crash-between-create-and-delete case where index lag is most likely"],"finding":"The self-cleaning label-SWEEP backstops (module finally-sweep in §2 and the workflow always-run acli sweep in §3) key on a JQL `labels = \"...\"` search, which is subject to the SAME Jira Cloud Lucene index lag §1 exists to defeat; in the crash window the backstop is meant to cover (a crash after create but before the by-key delete), the just-created issue may not yet be searchable, so the sweep returns empty and misses the very leak it exists to catch.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f85209f150cffb2e0","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"§2 (teardown 'sweeps any issue carrying THAT label') and §3 (acli `jira workitem search --jql \"labels = ...\"` then delete)","norm_id":"n7970d993cf9f055c","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A run crashes/cancels immediately after the throwaway issue's create, before the by-key delete; the label sweep's JQL search has not yet indexed the new issue and returns no hits, leaking the issue into shared REB — the exact failure the backstop is meant to prevent"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Route the module's finally-sweep through the §1 `wait_visible`-style poll (same schedule the coordinator re-observe uses) before deleting, and give the workflow's acli sweep a bounded retry loop around `acli jira workitem search` so an empty first result is re-polled rather than treated as 'nothing to sweep'.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5556,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] In §1, evaluate Atlassian's enhanced JQL Search API `reconcileIssues` parameter as prior art for the read-after-write/visibility problem (the codebase already POSTs to `/rest/api/3/search/jql` and the probe knows the created key), and justify the blind capped-exponential poll if reconcileIssues is rejected (e.g. acli client doesn't expose it, or the poll must also cover the by-key/property path).","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan §1 cites only the acli retry floor (`_errors.MAX_BACKOFF_S`) as prior art — for the backoff SHAPE, not for the root index-lag problem.","Atlassian docs (developer.atlassian.com REST v3 issue-search; community.atlassian.com): 'If you need read-after-write consistency, you can utilize the reconcileIssues parameter to ensure stronger consistency assurances' (up to 50 issue IDs).","Codebase already uses the enhanced endpoint: src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_graph.py POSTs to `/rest/api/3/search/jql` (lines ~260,299,388,471); tests reference the same path.","access_check.py:187 the probe holds `issue_key` (single created id) — exactly the input reconcileIssues consumes.","Problem statement asserts 'the write lands ... only SEARCH visibility lags' — the documented API remedy for precisely this is unevaluated."],"finding":"§1 hardens the JQL visibility wait with a blind capped-exponential poll (up to ~195s) but does not consider Atlassian's platform-native read-after-write remedy: the enhanced JQL Search API (`POST /rest/api/3/search/jql`) accepts a `reconcileIssues` parameter that returns consistent results for specified issue IDs (up to 50). The probe already knows the created issue key and the codebase already POSTs to `/rest/api/3/search/jql`, so this is directly available prior art for the very root cause (“SEARCH visibility lags”) the plan attacks by polling.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd29a077f5034c906","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"§1 — Harden the search-index wait (access_check.py)","norm_id":"n1928886688fb18be","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Live REB Cloud run where the create lands but the label JQL search lags: the plan burns up to 195s polling where a single reconcileIssues request could confirm visibility deterministically.","Future maintainers assume polling is the only option because §1's prior-art note only covers backoff shape."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add a sentence to §1 noting the `reconcileIssues` option: either adopt it (pass the just-created issue id to the search) to get deterministic read-after-write, or state why it is not used (e.g. the acli/direct-REST seam doesn't surface the parameter, or the probe must poll a label-based JQL not keyed to a single id) and keep the capped-exponential poll as the fallback.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"351eb662eb7ae718","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["f3b57a4ba80b8cd9",7989],"description_boxes":["7b70d3ab4c764154",7],"file_impact":["f57eb512a8fb0d03",11],"ticket_id":["b4b39ba2a98609cc",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":3690.6,"input_tokens":